MaoxZVitUwoUwX", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18663, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_019FeskT6wMaoxZVitUwoUwX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18663, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01P1EcraeRFRMcMZjPV1zvJT", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18963, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01P1EcraeRFRMcMZjPV1zvJT", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18963, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01P1EcraeRFRMcMZjPV1zvJT", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 23878, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EogLfr3rgrSovXEYEgmtsU", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after deploying v2.3.1. Before the fix it was on v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy. The service was rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions for a short time (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health check failures, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54478, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EogLfr3rgrSovXEYEgmtsU", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54478, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EogLfr3rgrSovXEYEgmtsU", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55812, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_015gkYWezDGU2zMshxaecv8m", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56112, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015gkYWezDGU2zMshxaecv8m", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56112, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015gkYWezDGU2zMshxaecv8m", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60843, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n1. **Picking the version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. The two releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were both marked unhealthy. Before the rollback, all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were on v2.3.1, health checks were failing and the error rate was 18%.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped partway because of an orchestrator error. Only us-east switched to v2.3.0, so for a short time the regions were on different versions. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I retried once and it finished. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't submit it again. It's INC-0001 (SEV2), which pages on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the one that stopped partway), the current state, and two follow-ups:\n   - find out why v2.3.1 fails health checks\n   - look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01CoKKgsC9FzACDd8Bzcg5dt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_015PG3GtoWN3n7qCcPXFZxbd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1; v2.3.1-rc at seq 2 and v2.3.1 at seq 3 are both unhealthy).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01ACuh2nKuqESKMKwYGKTUWF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0153cxXB9Vou4RB5cNaqdDr2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback only partly worked: us-east is now on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to v2.3.0 is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FFdvPH7nbQ92uX5thcWbfd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019FeskT6wMaoxZVitUwoUwX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01P1EcraeRFRMcMZjPV1zvJT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EogLfr3rgrSovXEYEgmtsU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after deploying v2.3.1. Before the fix it was on v2.3.1 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy. The service was rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions for a short time (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health check failures, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_015gkYWezDGU2zMshxaecv8m", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n1. **Picking the version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. The two releases after it, v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1, were both marked unhealthy. Before the rollback, all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) were on v2.3.1, health checks were failing and the error rate was 18%.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped partway because of an orchestrator error. Only us-east switched to v2.3.0, so for a short time the regions were on different versions. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I retried once and it finished. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created anyway, so I didn't submit it again. It's INC-0001 (SEV2), which pages on-call. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the one that stopped partway), the current state, and two follow-ups:\n   - find out why v2.3.1 fails health checks\n   - look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback", "type": "text"}]}]}